       ABI is used to perform a system call that takes  an  argument  of  type
       _i_n_t,  the  more‐significant half of the argument register is ignored by
       the system call, but visible in the seccomp data.

       A seccomp filter returns a 32‐bit value consisting of  two  parts:  the
       most significant 16 bits (corresponding to the mask defined by the con‐
       stant  SSEECCCCOOMMPP__RREETT__AACCTTIIOONN__FFUULLLL)  contain  one  of  the  "action" values
